{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Take heed, in the plague of tzara'at.</b> He warns that a person should not cut away the signs of a bright spot. But circumcision in a case of tzara'at — if the tzara'at was in the foreskin, they circumcise him and are not concerned. And so they said, of blessed memory: the positive commandment of circumcision comes and pushes aside the negative prohibition of tzara'at."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:50:46.283678718Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}